(693965, 72649, 13035, '<td valign="top">One of my favorites in the competition.  Good luck!!!  Normally I would argue with your placement of the people so low in the frame.  But in this case I think it only adds to your drama, and the proportion of this monolyth.  I just think it''s great.   I''m chearing for you for a ribbon.  9</td>', 'One of my favorites in the competition.  Good luck!!!  Normally I would argue with your placement of the people so low in the frame.  But in this case I think it only adds to your drama, and the proportion of this monolyth.  I just think it''s great.   I''m chearing for you for a ribbon.  9', '2004-05-02 19:18:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(693967, 71835, 13035, '<td valign="top">A ribbon winner in my competition.  Good luck!  I have the tiniest of suggestions.  Use clean ball.  jajaja.  I feel just a bit out of balance with the pitchers hand overlapping the border, but not foot.  I might try to keep them both inside frame, or both encroachiing.  Normally, I am not a fan of borders, but I think you have used one very effectively tying in your great title, and illustrating your concept.   Just great work.  9</td>', 'A ribbon winner in my competition.  Good luck!  I have the tiniest of suggestions.  Use clean ball.  jajaja.  I feel just a bit out of balance with the pitchers hand overlapping the border, but not foot.  I might try to keep them both inside frame, or both encroachiing.  Normally, I am not a fan of borders, but I think you have used one very effectively tying in your great title, and illustrating your concept.   Just great work.  9', '2004-05-02 19:23:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(693970, 72173, 13035, '<td valign="top">One of the strongest compositions of the contest, even though I don''t want an apartment anywhere near.   Contratulations on a fantastic urban theme.  I''m wondering about just the hint of water in the lower right.  I find myself wanting more or less, not quite sure.  I think that I might have cropped a little tighter.  I''m also finding myself wanting to know more about the skyline above.  I think I might have traded the water below, for more of the vista above.  Very nice shot.  Good luck!!!</td>', 'One of the strongest compositions of the contest, even though I don''t want an apartment anywhere near.   Contratulations on a fantastic urban theme.  I''m wondering about just the hint of water in the lower right.  I find myself wanting more or less, not quite sure.  I think that I might have cropped a little tighter.  I''m also finding myself wanting to know more about the skyline above.  I think I might have traded the water below, for more of the vista above.  Very nice shot.  Good luck!!!', '2004-05-02 19:30:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(693986, 72465, 13035, '<td valign="top">Very, very strong shot.  One of my ribbon choices.  Congratulations.  I might have composed with the tree just slightly more to the left.  In a competition that permitted spot editing, I would have removed some of the digital dust and reflective distractions in the dirt and front field.  There''s a distracting smudge in the sky about halfway up to the right of the tree.  Good luck!!! 9</td>', 'Very, very strong shot.  One of my ribbon choices.  Congratulations.  I might have composed with the tree just slightly more to the left.  In a competition that permitted spot editing, I would have removed some of the digital dust and reflective distractions in the dirt and front field.  There''s a distracting smudge in the sky about halfway up to the right of the tree.  Good luck!!! 9', '2004-05-02 19:49:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(693988, 72669, 13035, '<td valign="top">I''ve come to decide that this is the best in show.  Good luck!!!  I would crop out that tiny hint of the king that is visible tho the left of the center pawn.  It''s just a tad distracting.  Of course that''s not possible for the rules of this competition.  Just something to think about if you plan to take this image farther.  I would be entering everplace that I could find.  Great shot.  10</td>', 'I''ve come to decide that this is the best in show.  Good luck!!!  I would crop out that tiny hint of the king that is visible tho the left of the center pawn.  It''s just a tad distracting.  Of course that''s not possible for the rules of this competition.  Just something to think about if you plan to take this image farther.  I would be entering everplace that I could find.  Great shot.  10', '2004-05-02 19:51:50.000000', NULL, 1),
