(700413, 71835, 12735, '<td valign="top">Wow! I really like how this was set up. Congratulations!</td>', 'Wow! I really like how this was set up. Congratulations!', '2004-05-05 21:01:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(700475, 71835, 12448, '<td valign="top">OMG!  It looked soooooooooo real!  That is awesome!  WTG!<br/> <br/>Deannda</td>', 'OMG!  It looked soooooooooo real!  That is awesome!  WTG! Deannda', '2004-05-05 21:53:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(700491, 71835, 18191, '<td valign="top">I liked this shot...and i was glad that you didn''t use the technique willm used with his car shot...i was pretty sure you didnt strap on a tripod to the ball :)</td>', 'I liked this shot...and i was glad that you didn''t use the technique willm used with his car shot...i was pretty sure you didnt strap on a tripod to the ball :)', '2004-05-05 22:08:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(700492, 72032, 17175, '<td valign="top">Well, my favourite comment is "there is nothing to compare it too". Amazing. The head is disproportionate, the legs are disproportionate to the body, and I don''t need a penny next to the toy to get the idea that it''s substantially smaller than an actual pig. Plus, it''s very crisp and the mixture of pink and purple with the black and white background is very arty. Bravo! (applauds by tapping fingertips of right hand on flat of left palm)</td>', 'Well, my favourite comment is "there is nothing to compare it too". Amazing. The head is disproportionate, the legs are disproportionate to the body, and I don''t need a penny next to the toy to get the idea that it''s substantially smaller than an actual pig. Plus, it''s very crisp and the mixture of pink and purple with the black and white background is very arty. Bravo! (applauds by tapping fingertips of right hand on flat of left palm)', '2004-05-05 22:11:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(700519, 72050, 19930, '<td valign="top">I like this one. It finished one step lower than mine although I like your photo better!</td>', 'I like this one. It finished one step lower than mine although I like your photo better!', '2004-05-05 22:33:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(700738, 72105, 10275, '<td valign="top">Very very beautiful photo. great composition. one of my favs in this challenge.</td>', 'Very very beautiful photo. great composition. one of my favs in this challenge.', '2004-05-05 23:42:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(700762, 71835, 5792, '<td valign="top">Yours was a really nice setup and a deserving winner. Resourcefulness is the photographers best friend. Congrats on the clever image.</td>', 'Yours was a really nice setup and a deserving winner. Resourcefulness is the photographers best friend. Congrats on the clever image.', '2004-05-05 23:51:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(700799, 72800, 6943, '<td valign="top">Interesting picture, but I am curious as to how this relates to "proportion"?</td>', 'Interesting picture, but I am curious as to how this relates to "proportion"?', '2004-05-06 00:10:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(701012, 72729, 14012, '<td valign="top">**Critique Club**<br/> <br/>Hi Cybele -<br/> <br/>Great work on only your second entry at DPC. As stated below the colors and lines are great. It met the challenge very well.<br/> <br/>There is nothing that I can see to technically improve the shot. I personally would have liked a closer shot of the bee, but then you wouldn''t get the effect of "proportion" for the challenge, so you did right. The only other thing would be a crisper shot. I see a bit of noise and the photo is a bit soft overall. <br/> <br/>Overall, I think it is a great photo that you should be proud of. I look forward to seeing your future work.<br/> <br/>Regards,<br/>Chris<br/> <br/>Edit: corrected spelling<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-05-06 08:45:54.</i></td>', '**Critique Club** Hi Cybele - Great work on only your second entry at DPC. As stated below the colors and lines are great. It met the challenge very well. There is nothing that I can see to technically improve the shot. I personally would have liked a closer shot of the bee, but then you wouldn''t get the effect of "proportion" for the challenge, so you did right. The only other thing would be a crisper shot. I see a bit of noise and the photo is a bit soft overall.  Overall, I think it is a great photo that you should be proud of. I look forward to seeing your future work. Regards,Chris Edit: corrected spelling', '2004-05-06 01:55:05.000000', '2004-05-06 09:45:54.000000', 0),
(701035, 72649, 11181, '<td valign="top">Congrats!! You made it!! :)</td>', 'Congrats!! You made it!! :)', '2004-05-06 02:45:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(701039, 72653, 19780, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critque Club!<br/> <br/>Composition: The placement of the ladybug and the horizon of the egg in the upper third really helps to bring this together visually. As I stated during the competition, I''d like to see more of the egg - the title is really the only thing that tells me that it is an egg, I don''t know if it''d get that without it and I like the idea of the similarly shaped subjects. <br/> <br/>Background: Good neutral background keeps our eyes on the subject. <br/> <br/>Camera Work: (Focus/DOF/) the focus is just a little soft on the bug, I''d like to see the legs and head very crisp on this. DOF is spot on. <br/> <br/>Post Processing: n/a<br/> <br/>Appropriateness for the challenge: very - gives a sense of scale to both objects. More egg would help me. <br/> <br/>My Opinion: A very nice shot, pleasing and with a sense of whimsy. The colors are wonderful. I''ve seen a lot of ladybugs that are more orange lately in my yard and they wouldn''t have worked nearly as well as this wonderfully rich colored one. <br/> <br/>I hope these comments are of use to you, please note that if you can. Feel free to PM me or leave a note here if you have any other comments.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critque Club! Composition: The placement of the ladybug and the horizon of the egg in the upper third really helps to bring this together visually. As I stated during the competition, I''d like to see more of the egg - the title is really the only thing that tells me that it is an egg, I don''t know if it''d get that without it and I like the idea of the similarly shaped subjects.  Background: Good neutral background keeps our eyes on the subject.  Camera Work: (Focus/DOF/) the focus is just a little soft on the bug, I''d like to see the legs and head very crisp on this. DOF is spot on.  Post Processing: n/a Appropriateness for the challenge: very - gives a sense of scale to both objects. More egg would help me.  My Opinion: A very nice shot, pleasing and with a sense of whimsy. The colors are wonderful. I''ve seen a lot of ladybugs that are more orange lately in my yard and they wouldn''t have worked nearly as well as this wonderfully rich colored one.  I hope these comments are of use to you, please note that if you can. Feel free to PM me or leave a note here if you have any other comments.', '2004-05-06 02:51:01.000000', NULL, 0),
